ine to kill germs in drinking water.","art":"mf-3","source":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/cid/24526/record/JSON?record_type=3d","factSources":["https://www.cdc.gov/drinking-water/about/about-water-disinfection-with-chlorine-and-chloramine.html","https://www.epa.gov/ground-water-and-drinking-water/national-primary-drinking-water-regulations"],"factLicence":"US federal-authored factual references: public domain. Original Curio Class summary; no source prose or art copied.","geometrySource":"PubChem computed model"},{"name":"Hydrogen chloride","formula":"ClH","guideFormula":"HCl","cid":313,"atoms":["Cl","H"],"bonds":[[0,1,1]],"xyz":[[0,0,0],[60.58,-20.53,-113.84]],"fact":"In water it forms hydrochloric acid, the acid in your stomach.","art":"mf-4","source":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/cid/313/record/JSON?record_type=3d","factSources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D005744","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK535425/"],"factLicence":"Original factual summary only. US federal material is public domain; other publishers retain copyright. No outside prose, figures or tables copied. StatPearls: CC BY-NC-ND 4.0; factual reference only.","geometrySource":"PubChem computed model"},{"name":"Water","formula":"H2O","guideFormula":"H2O","cid":962,"atoms":["O","H","H"],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1]],"xyz":[[0,0,0],[27.74,89.29,25.44],[60.68,-23.83,-71.69]],"fact":"Water covers about 71 percent of Earth’s surface. Its molecule bends.","art":"mf-5","source":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/cid/962/record/JSON?record_type=3d","factSources":["https://www.usgs.gov/water-science-school/science/how-much-water-there-earth","https://www.nasa.gov/missions/aqua/when-it-comes-to-water-you-have-to-think-global/"],"factLicence":"USGS and NASA, US government public domain factual references. Original summary; no source images copied.","geometrySource":"PubChem computed model"},{"name":"Hydrogen sulfide","formula":"H2S","guideFormu